[en.PIHC_WS_C06_desc]
After the Las Pegasus resort being taken away by the cunning twins, Gladmane fled to Manehattan with a heart full of anger. In this city of money and sin, Gladmane rediscovered his talent and quickly became the new emerging mafia leader in the Manehattan area with his ability to form alliances. He attracted the attention of traditional political forces and patrons in the Manehattan area.
With the end of the Ultimate Battle, rumors of the “Big Three” coming to occupy Manehattan spread throughout the city. But when other ponies saw only fear, Gladmane saw opportunity. A great plan that could make him rise to the top gradually took shape in his mind.

In the spring of 1000, the reputation of the Las Pegasus Consortium became more and more famous in the Equestrian continent. The overambitious twins dared to expand their business to Manehattan. Gladmane took the lead in organizing a meeting and conspired with other mafia leaders to stop the twins from dumping Las Pegasus products in Manehattan. In the end, a driverless, unregistered, and “out-of-control” train loaded with explosives left Manehattan and headed slowly towards the train carrying goods to Manehattan from the twins...
The sensational “Ghost Train” accident in Equestria hit three birds with one stone: it not only destroyed the twins’ conspiracy to disrupt the Manehattan market, but also diverted the attention of the Equestria Unity Commission, and also blew up the core railway tunnel that connected Manehattan to the outside world. Due to the road blockage, Tirek and Cozy Glow also gave up the idea of attacking Manehattan and decided to leave it a future matter.
Gladmane’s success made him famous in the underground world of Manehattan. Among many traditional forces, Gladmane found his place, but his ambition was far from over.

For some reason, months passed, and there was no sign of the only railway tunnel from Manehattan to the outside world being repaired. Lacking supplies and political support from the outside world, the Manehattan city government quickly collapsed, and the dark underground world of Manehattan finally came to the surface. Manehattan has become a battlefield for open gang warfare. Gladmane, who had planned everything from the beginning, had already hoarded a large amount of weapons and ammunition. He watched as various gangs killed each other, while he sat quietly waiting to be pushed to the throne of power. Soon, Gladmane’s forces successfully took over the entire Manehattan. When the railway was repaired and Manehattan was finally reopened to the outside world, Gladmane’s name had already echoed in every dark alley in Manehattan.

Cozy Glow would not easily let go of the big prize that is Manehattan. As the fall of 1000 was coming to an end, when Manehattan finally reconnected with the outside world, the Equestria Empire immediately declared its jurisdiction over the Manehattan area, and Manehattan officially accepted the Empire’s jurisdiction. However, the three mayors appointed by the Empire were all assassinated, and the dozens of advisory groups sent by the Empire all became Gladmane’s loyal supporters after receiving a huge amount of “advisory fee”. In the summer of 1001, before the Empire could send the fourth mayor or any troops, Gladmane had already become the “elected” new mayor of Manehattan. Cozy Glow finally realized that when facing a pony like Gladmane, cooperation rather than confrontation seemed to be the solution to the problem.

[en.C06_DESC]


